<title>UK: UK drug sector up, takes cue from U.S. stocks.</title>
<headline>UK drug sector up, takes cue from U.S. stocks.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in the British drugs sector rose as they took their cue from steady pharmaceutical stocks in the U.S. overnight, analysts said.</p>
<p>Glaxo Wellcome led the pack, adding 11 pence to 1,161-1/2 by 0940 GMT, while SmithKline Beecham Plc, which will report its first-quarter results later today, advanced 12-1/2 pence to 918-1/2.</p>
<p>SmithKline is expected to announce pre-tax profits between 420 and 430 million stg, up from 387.0 million a year ago.</p>
<p>Zeneca shares gained 16-1/2 pence to 1,856.</p>
<p>-- London newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
